      "writtenOn": "2022-08-30T09:57:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "New comments explain why currentTimeMillis is not a good choice, but in a nutshell, the point is that in bug reports, we don\u0027t care what time the device clock was showing when the device first connected ; what matters is how long it\u0027s been connected, so we need a monotonic clock. Suppose you connect 5 minutes before daylight savings change the clock 1 hour back, you want to say the network has been connected for 5 minutes, not that it will connect in 55 minutes.",
      "parentUuid": "dea17190_6db6be2a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 199,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 199,
        "endChar": 47
